  "description": "Our little studio offers a convenient bolthole in Dublin 4. It is one of five apartments in a quiet Georgian-style house that is located at the Baggot Street end of tree-lined Waterloo Road. Within minutes of beautiful Herbert Park, and with all of the retail and restaurant amenities offered by Ballsbridge, it is also within close proximity of Dublin’s central business district. It is a lovely fifteen-minute walk from the house to St Stephen’s Green, and to Trinity College Dublin, and is a twenty-minute walk to the Grand Canal Dock area. The house is on a direct bus route to UCD. \n\nWaterloo Serviced Apartments offers serviced accommodation. Rates include Cable TV and Broadband and weekly housekeeping, that includes the weekly replacement of linens, and also household waste. \n\nFURNISHED, EQUIPPED AND SERVICED\n\nThe Bedroom/living room is furnished with a Japanese-style futon. Please note that this futon provides both the seating and the bed. An ottoman and storage case in the wardrobe provide storage for the bedclothes when these are not in use. There is a small fitted wardrobe; a TV cabinet and small TV complete the furniture. (A small desk and chair may be accommodated if wished.)\n\nThe fitted kitchen is equipped with a Bosch oven and hob, a fridge, and a full complement of tableware and cooking utensils. \n\nThe bathroom is fitted with a shower, a WC, and a hand basin with a large vanity unit. \n\nThe monthly cost includes Cable TV and Broadband, weekly housekeeping that comprises cleaning and bed linen change, and weekly replacement of towels. Household waste is also included. Electricity and heating are extra. A three-month minimum letting will apply – on enquiry, please be kind enough to provide some information about your requirements. Thank you for your interest. \n\n\n",
